# Model policy (Pro Plus) — quality + spend

**Plan assumption:** Cursor **Pro Plus** (~$60/mo) with **~$70/mo Other Models** API pool + generous **Cursor Models** pool (Composer / Grok family).

User upgraded from Auto-lock. Named models are allowed **except Grok**. Agents may remind the user which picker model to use; they cannot move the UI picker themselves.

## Default picker (email processing chat)

| Chat | Model picker | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **Email processing** (`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`) | **Recommended:** Claude 4.6 Sonnet (thinking). **User choice (2026-09-09): Auto** for higher case throughput — see user picker log in `.cursor/knowledge/pro-plus-model-spend-2026.md`. Composer if Other Models pacing is tight | German RE quality vs speed |
| **Instructions dashboard** (`AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS.md`) | **Pace-based** — see below | Maximize quality + month-end utilization of included pools |
| **September Incentive** | **Composer 2.5** (Sonnet only if bonus logic is unusually hard and Other Models has end-of-cycle headroom) | Light planning |

### Instructions dashboard — pace to ~max included usage (no on-demand)

**Philosophy:** Sweet spot = **high quality output** and **near-full use of included pools by billing-cycle end**. Minimizing usage is **not** the goal. Exceeding into on-demand is **forbidden** (on-demand stays Disabled).

| If… | Instructions chat should… |
|------|----------------------------|
| Behind pace (headroom + few days left) | Use **Claude 4.6 Sonnet** for complex rules/architecture tasks |
| On pace | **Composer 2.5** default; Sonnet for high-stakes multi-file changes |
| Ahead of pace / protect email RE budget | **Composer 2.5** only |
| Other Models exhausted | **Composer 2.5** only |

Remind the user to switch the picker when the task warrants it. Full pacing notes: `.cursor/knowledge/pro-plus-model-spend-2026.md` and `AGENT-INSTRUCTIONS.md`.

**Escalation (email chat):** **Claude 4.6 Opus** / **Opus 5** only for unusually hard cases. Switch back to Sonnet after.

**Email throughput when Other Models is scarce:** **Composer 2.5** on the email chat until the cycle resets.

## Hard ban — Grok

**Grok remains forbidden** for all Sprinklr case work (including Fast / 4.5 / 4.6 / `cursor-grok-*`).

If identity is Grok → STOP case work and output:

```
ERROR: GROK FORBIDDEN FOR CASE WORK.
Switch the model picker to Claude 4.6 Sonnet (or Composer 2.5), then resend.
```

## Subagents / Task tool

- Default `model`: **`"inherit"`** (or omit).
- Do **not** spawn Task/subagents to write the EMAIL **7-step RE** (hides text under background tasks). Parent agent writes sections 1–7 as visible chat.
- Subagents only for isolated repo research in the **instructions** chat.

## Quality + speed behaviours (case agent)

1. **Visible 7-step first**, then tools (play-ready / Auto-LF / arms).  
2. **Parallelize** independent tools (e.g. TransferMatrix grep + attachment open + KB) in one turn after CHANNEL: EMAIL.  
3. **Do not** re-extract or re-query KB when the current extract + matrix row already decide the path.  
4. Transfer-eligible: short §4a/5; skip deep solution hunting.  
5. Keep section 6 chat soft-wrap; PR paste stays mail-format.  
6. On Speichern pause: arm continue + `--await-speichern-continue` (no manual LF retry loop).

## Expected expenditure (Other Models pool)

Rates (Cursor docs, per **million** tokens) — **Claude 4.6 Sonnet**: input **$3**, cache read **~$0.30**, output **$15**.

### Per-case estimate (Sonnet, prompt-cache warm)

| Case type | Typical billable shape | Est. Other Models $ |
|-----------|------------------------|---------------------|
| EMAIL (RE + Auto-LF + PR + arm) | ~40–80k new input + heavy cache read + ~5–10k out + 2–4 follow-ups | **~$0.35–0.80** |
| CALL (CHANNEL + Auto-LF + Next) | Smaller context, fewer turns | **~$0.10–0.30** |
| Transfer-only EMAIL | Shorter §6 | **~$0.25–0.55** |

Composer 2.5 cases draw mainly from the **Cursor Models** pool (not the $70 Other pool) at Composer list rates — use when protecting Other Models budget.

### Monthly projection (Sonnet-primary)

Assume **20 workdays**, mix of EMAIL/CALL:

| Daily volume | Rough Other Models $/mo | vs Pro Plus **$70** included |
|--------------|-------------------------|------------------------------|
| 15 EMAIL + 10 CALL | ~$8–16 | Comfortable |
| 30 EMAIL + 20 CALL | ~$15–30 | Comfortable |
| 50 EMAIL + 30 CALL | ~$25–50 | OK; watch dashboard |
| 80 EMAIL + 40 CALL | ~$40–75 | Switch to Composer earlier — **do not** enable on-demand |

**Plus** $60 plan fee only. **On-demand usage must stay Disabled** (no overage charges). When included Other Models hits 100%, work continues on **Composer 2.5** (Cursor Models pool) or pauses until the cycle resets — never suggest enabling on-demand.

### On-demand = OFF (hard rule)

- User requirement: **on-demand / overage usage remains disabled**.
- Agent must **never** tell the user to enable on-demand, raise an overage limit, or “just turn on pay-as-you-go.”
- If included usage is exhausted or Cursor rate-limits: switch picker to **Composer 2.5**, or stop and wait for reset — do not bill beyond the plan.
- User verifies in Cursor: [Dashboard → Spending](https://cursor.com/dashboard/spending) → **On-Demand Usage** → Monthly Limit → **Disabled** (also: Settings → Plan & Usage → On-Demand → **Disabled**).

### Spend control

1. Check Cursor **Usage / Spending** mid-month (Other Models % vs Cursor Models).  
2. If Other Models > **~$45–50** (~65–70% of $70) before month-end → switch email chat to **Composer 2.5** for throughput; Sonnet/Opus only for sticky QA cases.  
3. Keep rules/incentive chats on Composer/Auto.  
4. Avoid Max Mode / 1M context unless a single case truly needs it.  
5. Do not run duplicate RE/`--once` for the same Fall # without cause.  
6. **Never** recommend on-demand, Ultra solely for overage headroom, or spend-limit increases.

## Identity check (every case turn)

- **Grok** → hard stop (error above).  
- **Claude Sonnet / Opus / Composer / GPT / Auto** → proceed.  
- If user asked for Sonnet but session is clearly a weak/wrong model for German RE, remind once: set picker to **Claude 4.6 Sonnet**.

## Honest limit

Rules cannot flip the Cursor model picker. The user must select **Claude 4.6 Sonnet** in the email processing chat after this policy change.
